{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0952"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c080): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c080.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0952"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge film-media/tv","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/film-media__tv.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",842],["+","The broadcast networks answered with mystery. Lost, created by J. J. Abrams, Damon Lindelof and Jeffrey Lieber, premiered on ABC on 22 September 2004 and followed the survivors of Oceanic Flight 815 on a strange Pacific island until its finale on 23 May 2010. Its puzzles became a national pastime: the numbers 4, 8, 15, 16, 23 and 42 – the numbers with which the character Hurley wins the lottery – turn up again and again in the series, so often that American fans began playing them in real lotteries.\n\n"],["=",134],["+","Lost | J. J. Abrams, Damon Lindelof, Jeffrey Lieber | ABC | 2004–2010 | Pacific island |\n| "],["=",91]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",842],["+","Die großen Networks antworteten mit dem Rätsel. Lost, erdacht von J. J. Abrams, Damon Lindelof und Jeffrey Lieber, startete am 22. September 2004 bei ABC und folgte den Überlebenden von Oceanic-Flug 815 auf einer seltsamen Pazifikinsel bis zum Finale am 23. Mai 2010. Ihre Rätsel wurden zum Volkssport: Die Zahlen 4, 8, 15, 16, 23 und 42 – mit denen die Figur Hurley im Lotto gewinnt – tauchen in der Serie immer wieder auf, so oft, dass amerikanische Fans sie schließlich als echte Lottozahlen spielten.\n\n"],["=",134],["+","Lost | J. J. Abrams, Damon Lindelof, Jeffrey Lieber | ABC | 2004–2010 | Pazifikinsel |\n| "],["=",91]]}]},
